From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: finish partial TX free batches

A truncated TX completion batch can be discovered after valid tokens have
already been released. Returning at that point skips the local skb free
list, the TX unblock flag and the TX worker. This can leak completed skbs
and leave transmissions stopped despite newly available tokens.

Finish the valid prefix through the normal completion epilogue instead.
Check the complete fixed header and every whole info word, including the
version 7 pair extension, before reading them. Pull a fragmented TXFREE
skb into linear storage before giving the full length to the parser.

The incomplete-batch warning was observed on an XR1710G NPU receive queue.
NPU/PPE forwarding, hardware queues and airtime limits are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>

--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1263,11 +1263,16 @@
 	struct mt76_wcid *wcid = NULL;
 	LIST_HEAD(free_list);
 	struct sk_buff *skb, *tmp;
-	void *end = data + len;
+	void *end;
 	bool wake = false;
 	u16 total, count = 0;
 	u8 ver;
 
+	if (len < 2 * (int)sizeof(*tx_free))
+		return;
+
+	end = data + len;
+
 	/* clean DMA queues and unmap buffers first */
 	mt76_queue_tx_cleanup(dev, dev->mphy.q_tx[MT_TXQ_PSD], false);
 	mt76_queue_tx_cleanup(dev, dev->mphy.q_tx[MT_TXQ_BE], false);
@@ -1289,8 +1294,8 @@
 		u32 msdu, info;
 		u8 i;
 
-		if (WARN_ON_ONCE((void *)cur_info >= end))
-			return;
+		if (WARN_ON_ONCE(end - (void *)cur_info < sizeof(*cur_info)))
+			break;
 		/* 1'b1: new wcid pair.
 		 * 1'b0: msdu_id with the same 'wcid pair' as above.
 		 */
@@ -1312,7 +1317,8 @@
 				goto next;
 next:
 			/* ver 7 has a new DW with pair = 1, skip it */
-			if (ver == 7 && ((void *)(cur_info + 1) < end) &&
+			if (ver == 7 &&
+			    end - (void *)(cur_info + 1) >= sizeof(*cur_info) &&
 			    (le32_to_cpu(*(cur_info + 1)) & MT_TXFREE_INFO_PAIR))
 				cur_info++;
 			continue;
@@ -1602,7 +1608,8 @@
 			break;
 		}
 
-		mt7996_mac_tx_free(dev, skb->data, skb->len);
+		if (pskb_may_pull(skb, skb->len))
+			mt7996_mac_tx_free(dev, skb->data, skb->len);
 		napi_consume_skb(skb, 1);
 		break;
 	case PKT_TYPE_RX_EVENT:
